      <data key="d100">Guanine nucleotide-binding protein G(q) subunit alpha</data>
      <data key="d101">Guanine nucleotide-binding protein alpha-q</data>
      <data key="d104">Guanine nucleotide-binding proteins (G proteins) function as transducers downstream of G protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs) in numerous signaling cascades. The alpha chain contains the guanine nucleotide binding site and alternates between an active, GTP-bound state and an inactive, GDP-bound state.</data>
